{"key":"db771616563f8932","source_file":"Potts N.json","source_id":37822,"source_url":"concordance-neptune-ppl-neptunus","term":"Neptune","headwords":["Neptune"],"latin":["Neptunus"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Neptune"],"latin":["Neptunus"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2762","subsection":"4"},"text":"When they described the god of the sea [Neptune], as by the sea are signified knowledges in general, they gave horses to him also. WH 4.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"159","subsection":"5"},"text":"See Apollo.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"178","subsection":null},"text":"From this it would follow... that the ocean is a god below them, who may be called Neptune...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"292","subsection":null},"text":"See Jupiter (the Roman god). SE 4775:2.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"neptune","url":"/meta/potts/neptune/"}